    "clinicalAlerts": "> [!WARNING]\n> • Patients with PAOD require education on risk factor management, exercise, and\n> pharmacologic treatment:\n> • Treatment of hyperlipidemia with a target LDL of <100 mg/dL\n> • Cessation of smoking\n> • Exercise, preferably walking\n> • Use of antiplatelet agents\n> • If surgical intervention for PAOD is indicated, arteriography or magnetic reso-\n> nance angiography is needed to determine the extent of the disease.\n> • Primary care providers should consider evaluation for carotid artery stenosis in\n> patients newly diagnosed with PAOD.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"test-27-anticardiolipin-antibody\"></a>",
