    "description": "Thyroglobulin is a thyroid glycoprotein that has a role in the synthesis of triiodothy-\nronine (T3) and thyroxine (T4). In some types of thyroid disorders, thyroglobulin may\nescape from the thyroid gland. Once liberated, these substances appear as antigens\nto the body. In response, the body produces antibodies against the thyroglobulin,\nleading to inflammation and destruction of the thyroid gland. Antithyroglobulin\nantibodies are present in the majority of patients diagnosed with Hashimoto’s thy-\nroiditis. The most dilute serum in which antithyroglobulin antibodies are detected\nis called the titer.",
