    "contributingFactors": "• The quality of the microscopic examination is highly dependent on the knowledge\nand experience of the individual performing the examination.\n• Hemolysis of specimen may alter test results.",
    "clinicalAlerts": "> [!WARNING]\n> • If blood smear is found to be abnormal, follow-up testing via bone marrow aspi-\n> ration or biopsy may be done.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"test-62-blood-typing-abo-typing-abo-red-cell-groups-blood-groups-rh-typing-type-and-crossmatch-t-c-type-and-screen\"></a>",
