    "contributingFactors": "• Levels of cortisol may vary with exercise, sleep, and stress.\n• Hemolysis of the sample may alter test results.\n• Drugs which may increase cortisol levels include: amphetamines, estrogens, ethyl\nalcohol, lithium carbonate, methadone, nicotine, oral contraceptives, spironolac-\ntone, synthetic glucocorticoids (prednisone, prednisolone).\n• Drugs which may decrease cortisol levels include: androgens, barbiturates, dexam-\nethasone, levodopa, phenytoin.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"test-109-cortisol-urine\"></a>",
