    "description": "Cystometrography (CMG), also known as cystometry is used to evaluate detrusor\nmuscle function and tone and to determine the cause of bladder dysfunction. The\ntest involves the instillation of fluid and/or air into the patient’s bladder.\nAssessments are made of the patient’s neurologic sensations and muscular\nresponses to this filling of the bladder. The patient’s voiding is also assessed for\nabnormalities. The results of this test are considered in conjunction with those of\nother urinary diagnostic tests, such as excretory urography and cystourethrography.\n\nCystourethrography involves the instillation of a contrast medium into the blad-\nder through a urethral catheter. As the bladder fills, x-ray films are taken. The\ncatheter is then removed and additional films are taken as the patient voids. This test\nis often used to evaluate patients who suffer from chronic urinary tract infections.",
