    "description": "This test is used to evaluate systemic fibrinolysis, to monitor thrombolytic therapy\nin patients with acute myocardial infarction, and to differentiate between primary\nfibrinolysis and disseminated intravascular coagulation (DIC) so that correct phar-\nmacologic therapy may be instituted.\n\nDuring hemostasis, thrombin stimulates the formation of fibrin from fibrinogen.\nThis fibrin, with the addition of fibrin stabilizing factor, forms a stable fibrin clot at\nthe site of injury. Once the fibrin clot is no longer needed, it is dissolved by fibri-\nnolytic agents such as plasmin, resulting in fibrin degradation products.\n\nWhen the body’s fibrinolytic system becomes overactive, any fibrin clot is dis-\nsolved as soon as it is formed, resulting in a bleeding disorder. This situation occurs\nwith primary fibrinolysis caused by such things as cancer of the prostate, shock,\nand administration of thrombolytic agents such as urokinase.",
