    "contributingFactors": "• Hemolysis of the blood sample and having a radioactive scan within 48 hours prior\nto the test will alter test results.\n• Strenuous exercise and stress may increase glucagon levels.\n• Receipt of radionuclide within 1 week may affect test results.\n• Drugs which may increase glucagon levels: arginine hydrochloride, danazol, gluco-\ncorticoids, gastrin, insulin, nifedipine.\n• Drugs which may decrease glucagon levels: atenolol, propranolol, secretin.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"test-170-glucose-blood-blood-sugar-fasting-blood-sugar-fbs-fasting-plasma-glucose-fpg\"></a>",
    "clinicalAlerts": "",
    "contraindications": ""
