    "contributingFactors": "• Voiding by males within 1 hour of a urethral culture may make fewer organisms\navailable for culture.\n• Douching by females within 24 hours of a cervical culture may make fewer organ-\nisms available for culture.\n• Use of lubricant can alter test results.",
    "clinicalAlerts": "> [!WARNING]\n> • Patients with positive test results should have their sexual partners examined.\n> • DNA testing using polymerase chain reaction (PCR) methodology is the newest\n> method of testing for gonorrhea. This can be done on a urine specimen. If used,\n> instruct the patient not to urinate for 1 hour prior to collection. The patient\n> should collect the first 15–50 mL of voided urine (the first part of the stream) in\n> a plastic, preservative-free, sterile urine collection cup.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"test-175-growth-hormone-growth-hormone-stimulation-suppression-test\"></a>",
