    "contributingFactors": "• Homocysteine levels can increase with age and with smoking.\n• Drugs that increase homocysteine levels: carbamazepine, cycloserine, isoniazid,\nmethotrexate, penicillamine, phenytoin, procarbazine.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"test-188-human-leukocyte-antigen-test-hla-test-hla-typing-histocompatibility-antigen-test-tissue-typing\"></a>",
