    "category": "Immunology & Serology",
    "description": "Human T-cell lymphotrophic virus (HTLV) is the name for several different retro-\nviruses. HTLV-III is the former name of the human immunodeficiency virus (HIV)\nknown to cause acquired immunodeficiency syndrome (AIDS). HTLV-I and HTLV-II\ndo not cause AIDS. They are, however, associated with other types of diseases.\nHTLV-I is linked with adult T-cell leukemia. HTLV-II is associated with adult hairy-\ncell leukemia. However, presence of the antibody to these viruses in the blood does\nnot necessarily mean the person will develop the disease.",
