    "decreased": [],
    "abnormalFindings": [],
    "contributingFactors": "",
    "clinicalAlerts": "> [!WARNING]\n> • Workers exposed to lead should have blood lead levels <40 µg/dL.\n> • In children with blood lead levels >10 µg/mL, the source of the lead exposure\n> must be identified and removed. Treatment is needed for levels >25 µg/dL.\n> • Red blood cell studies usually show a microcytic anemia when lead poisoning is\n> present.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"test-207-legionnaire-s-disease-antibody-test\"></a>",
