    "description": "Lesions of the lung may be studied through such tests as chest x-ray, computed\ntomography (CT) scan, and bronchoscopy. However, determination of the nature of a\nlesion, that is, whether a mass is benign or malignant, can only be made by obtain-\ning a biopsy of the tissue. In a lung biopsy, a sample of lung tissue is removed for\nhistologic study. The tissue sample may be obtained by needle biopsy through the\nchest wall, by tissue sampling during fiberoptic bronchoscopy, or by open biopsy dur-\ning a thoracotomy. This discussion will be limited to that of needle biopsy of the lung.",
