    "description": "Lymphangiography is the term used to indicate visualization of the lymphatic system.\nA contrast medium is injected into each foot. Visualization is then possible of the lym-\nphatic system from the feet up to the thoracic duct. The test is used to detect and\nstage lymphomas and to assist in the differential diagnosis of lymphedema. When\nused with lymph node biopsy, the lymphangiogram can be used to determine the pos-\nsible spread of cancer and effectiveness of cancer therapy. The contrast medium\nremains in the body for 1 to 2 years, thus allowing subsequent films to be made in\norder to monitor disease progression and assess any response of the patient to therapy.",
