    "category": "Urinalysis & Renal Clearance",
    "description": "The urine osmolality measures the number of osmotically active particles in the\nurine, or the concentration of the urine. This, in turn, reflects the ability of the kid-\nneys to concentrate urine. The test is useful in assessing fluid and electrolyte imbal-\nances and in determining fluid requirements. It is especially useful in the evaluation\nof hyponatremia and hypernatremia, and to distinguish prerenal azotemia from\nischemic acute tubular necrosis. Following an overnight fast, the urine osmolality\nshould be at least three times the osmolality of the blood.",
