    "clinicalAlerts": "> [!WARNING]\n> • Serum phosphorus results should be correlated with serum calcium levels to\n> determine possible causes.\n> • Increased phosphorus with decreased calcium: hypoparathyroidism, renal\n> disease\n> • Increased phosphorus with normal or increased calcium: milk-alkali syndrome,\n> hypervitaminosis D\n> • Decreased phosphorus with increased calcium: hyperparathyroidism, sarcoidosis\n> • Decreased phosphorus and calcium: malabsorption, vitamin D deficiency,\n> renal tubular acidosis\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"test-253-plasminogen\"></a>",
