    "contributingFactors": "• Hemolysis of the blood sample or having a radioactive scan within 1 week of the test\nmay alter test results.\n• Drugs which may increase progesterone levels: adrenocortical hormones,\nclomiphene, estrogens, ketoconazole, progesterones, tamoxifen.\n• Drugs which may decrease progesterone levels: ampicillin, anticonvulsants, dana-\nzol, goserelin, leuprolide, oral contraceptives.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"test-273-prolactin-level-prl-human-prolactin-hprl-lactogen-lactogenic-hormone\"></a>",
