    "clinicalAlerts": "> [!WARNING]\n> • If the rapid strep test is positive, the patient needs to be treated with an antibi-\n> otic, such as penicillin or, if allergic to penicillin, erythromycin.\n> • If the rapid strep test is negative, a follow-up culture and sensitivity test is con-\n> ducted to determine whether the rapid strep test result was a false negative\n> result. It may take several days before the final culture report is available.\n> • A positive test result does not differentiate between individuals with an active\n> strep infection and those who are carriers of strep bacteria who may currently\n> have a viral infection.",
