    "description": "Renal biopsy, in which a sample of renal tissue is obtained for histologic study, is used\nto aid in the diagnosis of renal parenchymal disease. The tissue sample may be\nobtained by percutaneous needle biopsy through the skin, or by open biopsy through a\nsurgical incision. This discussion will be limited to that of needle biopsy of the kidney.\n\nRenal biopsy can be used in the diagnosis of such conditions as glomeru-\nlonephritis, pyelonephritis, and systemic lupus erythematosus. Considering the risk\nof damage to the kidney tissue during biopsy and the availability of alternative diag-\nnostic tests such as ultrasonography and computer tomography (CT), the risk-\nbenefit of performing this test must be carefully weighed.",
