    "contributingFactors": "Drugs that may cause false-negative results: antibiotics, barium, bismuth, mineral oil.",
    "clinicalAlerts": "> [!WARNING]\n> • Patients complaining of diarrhea for at least 2 weeks usually have stool analysis\n> performed, often including stool for WBCs, stool culture, stool for ova and para-\n> sites, Clostridium difficile, and possibly Giardia.\n> • Follow-up stool analysis may be done if symptoms persist despite initial stool tests hav-\n> ing negative results, or to demonstrate the pathogen is no longer present in the stool.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"test-311-stool-for-occult-blood-fecal-occult-blood-test-fobt-fecal-immunochemical-test-fit\"></a>",
    "contraindications": ""
