    "category": "Blood Chemistry & Metabolism",
    "description": "Thoracoscopy is a procedure in which small incisions are made in the chest wall\nand a thoracoscope is inserted. This procedure allows the physician to examine the\nparietal and visceral pleura, mediastinum, and pericardium. The procedure is done\nto obtain tissue and fluid samples, diagnose and stage cancer, remove fluid, and\nintroduce medications into the pleural cavity. Although it is considered a surgical\nprocedure, thoracoscopy results in a shorter hospital and recovery time than would\noccur with thoracotomy.",
