    "clinicalAlerts": "> [!WARNING]\n> • In iron deficiency anemia, iron is low and TIBC is increased, resulting in very low\n> transferrin saturation.\n> • In iron overload, as seen with hemochromatosis, iron is high and TIBC is low or\n> normal, resulting in high transferrin saturation.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"test-332-toxicology-screen\"></a>",
