    "contributingFactors": "• Drugs that can increase T3uptake (T3U)values: anabolic steroids, barbiturates, cor-\nticosteroids, furosemide, heparin, phenylbutazone, phenytoin, salicylates, thyrox-\nine, warfarin.\n• Drugs that can decrease T3U values: antithyroid agents, clofibrate, estrogens, oral\ncontraceptives, thiazide diuretics.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"test-340-troponin\"></a>",
