    "clinicalAlerts": "> [!WARNING]\n> • If the BUN is elevated, check with the primary care provider prior to administer-\n> ing any nephrotoxic medication.\n> • Before receiving intravascular iodinated contrast material, patients meeting one or\n> more of the following criteria should have BUN and creatinine testing completed:\n> • Known creatinine level ≥1.5\n> • Age 60 and over\n> • Personal or family history of renal disease\n> • Personal history of diabetes mellitus\n> • History of collagen vascular disease, such as lupus\n> • Currently taking certain medications: metformin, nephrotoxic antibiotics\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"test-344-uric-acid-blood\"></a>",
