    "category": "Imaging & Procedures",
    "description": "Uroflowmetry is a noninvasive procedure which is used to detect dysfunctional void-\ning patterns. The test includes the measurement of the voiding duration, amount,\nand rate using a urine flowmeter, an instrument into which the patient voids. For\n\nthe most accurate evaluation of urine flow patterns, recording of each voiding for\n2 to 3 days should be performed. Uroflowmetry is usually performed in conjunction\nwith other urinary tract testing, such as cystometry. Although the urethral pressure\nprofile test is more often used, uroflowmetry is useful for testing patients in whom\nurinary catheterization is contraindicated.",
